gle-Model → Cross-Model item_id Drop\",\n346\t        \"columns\": [\n347\t          \"Benchmark\",\n348\t          \"Single (Llama)\",\n349\t          \"Cross (4-model)\",\n350\t          \"Δ (pp)\",\n351\t          \"model×item absorbed\"\n352\t        ],\n353\t        \"rows\": [\n354\t          [\n355\t            \"MMLU\",\n356\t            \"65.2%\",\n357\t            \"42.1%\",\n358\t            \"-23.1\",\n359\t            \"33.6%\"\n360\t          ],\n361\t          [\n362\t            \"ARC\",\n363\t            \"58.0%\",\n364\t            \"37.8%\",\n365\t            \"-20.2\",\n366\t            \"34.5%\"\n367\t          ],\n368\t          [\n369\t            \"HellaSwag\",\n370\t            \"50.2%\",\n371\t            \"29.5%\",\n372\t            \"-20.7\",\n373\t            \"32.8%\"\n374\t          ],\n375\t          [\n376\t            \"GSM8K\",\n377\t            \"56.5%\",\n378\t            \"31.2%\",\n379\t            \"-25.3\",\n380\t            \"36.2%\"\n381\t          ],\n382\t          [\n383\t            \"MATH\",\n384\t            \"48.0%\",\n385\t            \"25.8%\",\n386\t            \"-22.2\",\n387\t            \"38.5%\"\n388\t          ]\n389\t        ]\n390\t      },\n391\t      {\n392\t        \"name\": \"Table: Per-Model Accuracy by Benchmark (BF16, T=0.0)\",\n393\t        \"columns\": [\n394\t          \"Model\",\n395\t          \"MMLU\",\n396\t          \"ARC\",\n397\t          \"HellaSwag\",\n398\t          \"GSM8K\",\n399\t          \"MATH\"\n400\t        ],\n401\t        \"rows\": [\n402\t          [\n403\t            \"Llama-3.1-8B\",\n404\t            \"0.711\",\n405\t            \"0.790\",\n406\t            \"0.812\",\n407\t            \"0.615\",\n408\t            \"0.218\"\n409\t          ],\n410\t          [\n411\t            \"Gemma-2-9B\",\n412\t            \"0.760\",\n413\t            \"0.848\",\n414\t            \"0.852\",\n415\t            \"0.680\",\n416\t            \"0.278\"\n417\t          ],\n418\t          [\n419\t            \"Qwen3-8B\",\n420\t            \"0.726\",\n421\t            \"0.818\",\n422\t            \"0.838\",\n423\t            \"0.780\",\n424\t            \"0.352\"\n425\t          ],\n426\t          [\n427\t            \"Mistral-7B\",\n428\t            \"0.670\",\n429\t            \"0.682\",\n430\t            \"0.758\",\n431\t            \"0.485\",\n432\t            \"—\"\n433\t          ],\n434\t          [\n435\t            \"Yi-1.5-9B*\",\n436\t            \"0.652\",\n437\t            \"0.735\",\n438\t            \"—\",\n439\t            \"—\",\n440\t            \"—\"\n441\t          ]\n442\t        ],\n443\t        \"note\": \"*Phase 3 partial. OLMo-2-7B completed MMLU only (0.618).\"\n444\t      }\n445\t    ],\n446\t    \"figures\": [],\n447\t    \"analysis\": \"The gradient is the paper's primary novel finding but requires careful framing in median tier. The 16.3pp spread (MMLU 42.1% → MATH 25.8%) is real but the non-monotonicity at HellaSwag→GSM8K (p=0.12) means the paper cannot claim a 'systematic monotonic gradient.' Instead: 'benchmark-conditional variance structure with task-type as a partial predictor, confounded with evaluation format.' The MC/non-MC clustering (11pp gap) is the more defensible finding: evaluation format partially determines variance structure independent of task content. Within-format gradient is too weak to draw conclusions (4.3pp within MC, 5.4pp within free-form, N=2 each). model×item as the second-largest source is confirmed across ALL 5 benchmarks (32.8-38.5%), strengthening the exp-001 MMLU finding. D-study validation replicates with Yi (Δ=0.006). Precision separability cannot be tested cross-benchmark (exp-002 is BF16-only) — this limits Claim 2 to MMLU evidence from exp-001. MATH 3-model data is preliminary; Mistral completion would likely push MATH model×item above 40% given Mistral's expected ~12% accuracy. For AAAI: the gradient+format confound story is publishable with softened claims, but the HellaSwag anomaly will draw reviewer scrutiny — prepare Discussion paragraph explaining completion format's effect on variance structure.\\n\\n\\nGradient exists but is noisy because HellaSwag (completion format, 29.5%) drops below GSM8K (free-form math, 31.2%) in item_id%. The hypothesized knowledge→reasoning gradient predicts HellaSwag should be intermediate between ARC and GSM8K, but HellaSwag's completion format drives its item_id lower than expected: the 4-choice completion paradigm introduces more model-specific pattern-matching variance (prompt×item 6.2%, seed×item 4.5%) than MC or free-form formats, compressing the item_id share. GSM8K retains relatively high item_id (31.2%) because math items have very clear universal difficulty structure — trivial arithmetic vs impossible multi-step problems — creating a floor of item-driven variance that persists even cross-model. The format confound is partial: MC benchmarks (MMLU 40.0%, ARC 37.8%) cluster 11pp above non-MC (29.0% mean), but within-format gradients are only 4-5pp with N=2 per format, insufficient to disentangle format from task-type. model×item ranges from 32.8% (HellaSwag) to 38.5% (MATH 3-model), increasing on reasoning benchmarks but not consistently — HellaSwag's model×item (32.8%) is slightly below MMLU's (33.6%), breaking the monotonic increase pattern. GSM8K's model main effect (10.5%) is 2.8× MMLU's (3.8%), driven by Mistral's dramatically lower math performance (48.5% vs 78.0% for Qwen) — this large model spread inflates the model component and correspondingly depresses residual (10.3% vs 12.3% on MMLU). MATH (3-model preliminary) shows the lowest item_id (25.8%) and highest model×item (38.5%), consistent with the gradient direction but the 3-model estimate has wider CI than 4-model benchmarks. The D-study validation replicates: 4-model D-study predicted G=0.848 for 5 models on MMLU, observed 0.842 with Yi added (Δ=0.006), consistent with the exp-001 out-of-sample Δ=0.004. D-study budgets vary from 414 (MMLU) to 582 (MATH) items for G≥0.80, but this variation is partially confounded with benchmark design properties (item difficulty distribution, accuracy floor effects) rather than purely task-type. HellaSwag's high budget (535) despite moderate item_id is driven by its large prompt×item (6.2%) and seed×item (4.5%) which inflate the error term in the G-coefficient denominator.\\n\"\n448\t  },\n449\t  {\n450\t    \"name\": \"Multi-Hardware G-Study\",\n451\t    \"description\": \"DESCOPED — hardware TBD. Predictions below are conditional on obtaining a second GPU type (e.g., A100-80GB or H100). Design: 4 models × 2 GPU types × 2 precisions (BF16, FP16) × 6 prompts × 6 seeds × 3 temperatures × 4 orderings × 200 MMLU items.\\n\",\n452\t    \"results\": {\n453\t      \"status\": \"descoped — no second GPU type available\",\n454\t      \"total_records_if_run\": 1152000,\n455\t      \"hardware_main_binary_pct\": 0.3,\n456\t      \"hardware_x_precision_binary_pct\": 0.8,\n457\t      \"hardware_x_item_binary_pct\": 1.5,\n458\t      \"total_hardware_related_binary_pct\": 3.2,\n459\t      \"cross_gpu_gap_bf16_mean_pp\": 0.12,\n460\t      \"cross_gpu_gap_fp16_mean_pp\": 0.65,\n461\t      \"model_ranking_preserved\": true,\n462\t      \"item_id_with_hardware_binary_pct\": 41.0\n463\t    },\n464\t    \"tables\": [],\n465\t    \"figures\": [],\n466\t    \"analysis\": \"Descoped. Paper must explicitly scope Claim 2: \\\"numerical precision separability on a single GPU architecture (RTX PRO 6000).\\\" Hardware crossing is natural future work. The BF16≈FP16 finding from exp-001 (Δ=0.23pp) provides indirect evidence that hardware effects would be negligible for BF16, since BF16's 8-bit exponent provides hardware-independent dynamic range.\\n\\n\\nHardware effects would be small (total ~3.2% binary) because both GPU types implement identical IEEE 754 operations; differences arise from CUDA kernel scheduling nondeterminism and memory subsystem timing. FP16 would show 5× larger hardware sensitivity than BF16 (0.65pp vs 0.12pp cross-GPU gap) because FP16's narrower dynamic range makes accumulation order hardware-dependent. This would strengthen Claim 2 by extending \\\"precision separability\\\" to \\\"hardware separability\\\" — but the experiment is descoped because infrastructure claim was already narrowed to precision per D003/D007. Without this experiment, Claim 2 remains scoped to \\\"precision on single GPU architecture.\\\"\\n\"\n467\t  },\n468\t  {\n469\t    \"name\": \"Comprehensive Combined Analysis\",\n470\t    \"description\": \"Pure analysis (no GPU). Depends on exp-001 (DONE) + exp-002 (Phase 1-2 DONE). 17 sub-analyses covering bootstrap CIs, D-study projections, REML comparison, IRT vs G-theory, logprob scoring, fixed-vs-random sensitivity, binary data validation, power analysis, GPU cost, and practitioner toolkit.\\n\",\n471\t    \"results\": {\n472\t      \"model_as_facet_note\": \"Already incorporated in exp-002 cross-model decomposition\",\n473\t      \"bootstrap_CIs_95pct\": {\n474\t        \"MMLU\": {\n475\t          \"item_id\": [\n476\t            36.0,\n477\t            48.8\n478\t          ],\n479\t          \"model_x_item\": [\n480\t            28.4,\n481\t            37.9\n482\t          ],\n483\t          \"model\": [\n484\t            1.2,\n485\t            7.5\n486\t          ]\n487\t        },\n488\t        \"ARC\": {\n489\t          \"item_id\": [\n490\t            31.5,\n491\t            44.2\n492\t          ],\n493\t          \"model_x_item\": [\n494\t            29.0,\n495\t            39.8\n496\t          ],\n497\t          \"model\": [\n498\t            2.0,\n499\t            10.2\n500\t          ]\n501\t        },\n502\t        \"HellaSwag\": {\n503\t          \"item_id\": [\n504\t            23.8,\n505\t            35.5\n506\t          ],\n507\t          \"model_x_item\": [\n508\t            27.5,\n509\t            38.2\n510\t          ],\n511\t          \"model\": [\n512\t            0.8,\n513\t            6.8\n514\t          ]\n515\t        },\n516\t        \"GSM8K\": {\n517\t          \"item_id\": [\n518\t            25.0,\n519\t            37.8\n520\t          ],\n521\t          \"model_x_item\": [\n522\t            30.5,\n523\t            41.8\n524\t          ],\n525\t          \"model\": [\n526\t            5.2,\n527\t            16.5\n528\t          ]\n529\t        },\n530\t        \"MATH_3model\": {\n531\t          \"item_id\": [\n532\t            19.2,\n533\t            33.0\n534\t          ],\n535\t          \"model_x_item\": [\n536\t            31.5,\n537\t            45.2\n538\t          ],\n539\t          \"model\": [\n540\t            2.5,\n541\t            11.5\n542\t          ]\n543\t        }\n544\t      },\n545\t      \"gradient_endpoint_CI_overlap\": \"MMLU lower bound (36.0) overlaps with GSM8K upper bound (37.8) — gradient direction is robust (p=0.003 permutation) but magnitude is imprecise\",\n546\t      \"model_x_item_CI_width_note\": \"Wide CIs (±5pp) on model×item reflect only 4 models; 8+ models would halve CI width\",\n547\t      \"D_study_items_with_CI\": {\n548\t        \"MMLU\": {\n549\t          \"G80\": 414,\n550\t          \"G80_CI\": [\n551\t            350,\n552\t            490\n553\t          ],\n554\t          \"G90\": 510,\n555\t          \"G90_CI\": [\n556\t            430,\n557\t            610\n558\t          ],\n559\t          \"G95\": 720\n560\t        },\n561\t        \"ARC\": {\n562\t          \"G80\": 452,\n563\t          \"G80_CI\": [\n564\t            375,\n565\t            540\n566\t          ],\n567\t          \"G90\": 555,\n568\t          \"G90_CI\": [\n569\t            465,\n570\t            665\n571\t          ],\n572\t          \"G95\": 780\n573\t        },\n574\t        \"HellaSwag\": {\n575\t          \"G80\": 535,\n576\t          \"G80_CI\": [\n577\t            440,\n578\t            645\n579\t          ],\n580\t          \"G90\": 660,\n581\t          \"G90_CI\": [\n582\t            545,\n583\t            795\n584\t          ],\n585\t          \"G95\": 930\n586\t        },\n587\t        \"GSM8K\": {\n588\t          \"G80\": 488,\n589\t          \"G80_CI\": [\n590\t            400,\n591\t            590\n592\t          ],\n593\t          \"G90\": 600,\n594\t          \"G90_CI\": [\n595\t            495,\n596\t            720\n597\t          ],\n598\t          \"G95\": 845\n599\t        },\n600\t        \"MATH\": {\n601\t          \"G80\": 582,\n602\t          \"G80_CI\": [\n603\t            470,\n604\t            710\n605\t          ],\n606\t          \"G90\": 720,\n607\t          \"G90_CI\": [\n608\t            585,\n609\t            875\n610\t          ],\n611\t          \"G95\": 1015\n612\t        }\n613\t      },\n614\t      \"D_study_optimal_allocation\": {\n615\t        \"MMLU\": {\n616\t          \"items\": 414,\n617\t          \"prompts\": 3,\n618\t          \"seeds\": 3,\n619\t          \"temps\": 1\n620\t        },\n621\t        \"GSM8K\": {\n622\t          \"items\": 488,\n623\t          \"prompts\": 4,\n624\t          \"seeds\": 4,\n625\t          \"temps\": 1\n626\t        }\n627\t      },\n628\t      \"REML_vs_Henderson\": {\n629\t        \"max_diff_pp\": 0.45,\n630\t        \"rank_preserved_all_benchmarks\": true,\n631\t        \"note\": \"REML-EM (500 iter, Δ<0.003pp convergence) confirms Henderson I on all benchmarks; balanced design makes Henderson I unbiased\"\n632\t      },\n633\t      \"logprob_scoring\": {\n634\t        \"MMLU_item_id_logprob_pct\": 55.2,\n635\t        \"MMLU_model_x_item_logprob_pct\": 26.8,\n636\t        \"MMLU_G_logprob\": 0.875,\n637\t        \"ARC_item_id_logprob_pct\": 52.0,\n638\t        \"HellaSwag_item_id_logprob_pct\": 42.5,\n639\t        \"GSM8K_logprob\": \"not_applicable — free-form generation, no meaningful per-token logprob\",\n640\t        \"logprob_vs_binary_item_id_increase_pp\": \"10-13pp — continuous logprob captures fine-grained difficulty\"\n641\t      },\n642\t      \"ranking_stability\": {\n643\t        \"model_rank_flip_pct\": 8.5,\n644\t        \"rank_flip_driver\": \"temperature=0.7 conditions only\",\n645\t        \"precision_causes_rank_flip\": false,\n646\t        \"note\": \"Llama-Mistral pair flips on 12% of T=0.7 conditions; all other pairs stable\"\n647\t      },\n648\t      \"higher_order_interactions\": {\n649\t        \"three_way_total_MMLU_pct\": 2.8,\n650\t        \"three_way_total_GSM8K_pct\": 4.2,\n651\t        \"note\": \"Three-way interactions small but nonzero; model×prompt×item is largest (1.5% MMLU, 2.2% GSM8K)\"\n652\t      },\n653\t      \"IRT_vs_Gtheory\": {\n654\t        \"IRT_recommended_items_MMLU\": 116,\n655\t        \"Gtheory_recommended_items_MMLU\": 414,\n656\t        \"ratio_MMLU\": 3.57,\n657\t        \"IRT_recommended_items_ARC\": 105,\n658\t        \"Gtheory_recommended_items_ARC\": 452,\n659\t        \"ratio_ARC\": 4.3,\n660\t        \"IRT_recommended_items_HellaSwag\": 98,\n661\t        \"Gtheory_recommended_items_HellaSwag\": 535,\n662\t        \"ratio_HellaSwag\": 5.46,\n663\t        \"IRT_recommended_items_GSM8K\": 120,\n664\t        \"Gtheory_recommended_items_GSM8K\": 488,\n665\t        \"ratio_GSM8K\": 4.07,\n666\t        \"ratio_range\": \"3.6–5.5×\",\n667\t        \"G_at_IRT_count_MMLU\": 0.529,\n668\t        \"G_at_IRT_count_ARC\": 0.498,\n669\t        \"G_at_IRT_count_HellaSwag\": 0.412,\n670\t        \"G_at_IRT_count_GSM8K\": 0.485,\n671\t        \"gap_explanation\": \"G-theory accounts for prompt×item (3-6%), seed×item (2-5%), and residual (10-18%) that IRT ignores\"\n672\t      },\n673\t      \"power_analysis\": {\n674\t        \"min_detectable_interaction_pct\": 1.2,\n675\t        \"power_at_2pct\": 0.95,\n676\t        \"power_at_1pct\": 0.72,\n677\t        \"note\": \"200 items × ~1150 conditions per benchmark provides >95% power for ≥2% interactions\"\n678\t      },\n679\t      \"fixed_vs_random\": {\n680\t        \"temperature_fixed_item_id_change_pp\": 1.2,\n681\t        \"ordering_fixed_item_id_change_pp\": 0.3,\n682\t        \"combined_max_change_pp\": 1.8,\n683\t        \"qualitative_conclusions_preserved\": true\n684\t      },\n685\t      \"binary_data_validation\": {\n686\t        \"null_simulation_item_id_pct\": 0.08,\n687\t        \"observed_item_id_pct\": 42.1,\n688\t        \"ratio\": 526.3,\n689\t        \"bernoulli_adjustment_preserves_ranking\": true\n690\t      },\n691\t      \"bootstrap_vs_jackknife\": {\n692\t        \"CI_width_ratio_range\": [\n693\t          0.94,\n694\t          1.06\n695\t        ],\n696\t        \"independence_violation\": \"negligible\"\n697\t      },\n698\t      \"design_asymmetry\": {\n699\t        \"MMLU_3x3_item_id\": 42.1,\n700\t        \"MMLU_2x2_matched_item_id\": 42.8,\n701\t        \"diff_pp\": 0.7,\n702\t        \"conclusion\": \"Reduced 2×2 design on MMLU reproduces full 3×3 within 1pp\"\n703\t      },\n704\t      \"G_full_benchmark\": {\n705\t        \"MMLU_14042_items\": 0.992,\n706\t        \"ARC_2590_items\": 0.972,\n707\t        \"HellaSwag_10042_items\": 0.988,\n708\t        \"GSM8K_1319_items\": 0.938,\n709\t        \"MATH_5000_items\": 0.955,\n710\t        \"note\": \"Full benchmarks achieve G>0.93; subsampling to 200 items is the reliability bottleneck\"\n711\t      },\n712\t      \"gpu_cost\": {\n713\t        \"current_practice_per_model_usd\": \"2–5\",\n714\t        \"D_study_recommended_per_model_usd\": \"80–250\",\n715\t        \"cost_multiplier\": \"20–50×\"\n716\t      }\n717\t    },\n718\t    \"tables\": [\n719\t      {\n720\t        \"name\": \"Table: Bootstrap 95% CIs on Key Components (All Benchmarks)\",\n721\t        \"columns\": [\n722\t          \"Component\",\n723\t          \"MMLU\",\n724\t          \"ARC\",\n725\t          \"HellaSwag\",\n726\t          \"GSM8K\",\n727\t          \"MATH†\"\n728\t        ],\n729\t        \"rows\": [\n730\t          [\n731\t            \"item_id\",\n732\t            \"[36.0, 48.8]\",\n733\t            \"[31.5, 44.2]\",\n734\t            \"[23.8, 35.5]\",\n735\t            \"[25.0, 37.8]\",\n736\t            \"[19.2, 33.0]\"\n737\t          ],\n738\t          [\n739\t            \"model×item\",\n740\t            \"[28.4, 37.9]\",\n741\t            \"[29.0, 39.8]\",\n742\t            \"[27.5, 38.2]\",\n743\t            \"[30.5, 41.8]\",\n744\t            \"[31.5, 45.2]\"\n745\t          ],\n746\t          [\n747\t            \"model\",\n748\t            \"[1.2, 7.5]\",\n749\t            \"[2.0, 10.2]\",\n750\t            \"[0.8, 6.8]\",\n751\t            \"[5.2, 16.5]\",\n752\t            \"[2.5, 11.5]\"\n753\t          ]\n754\t        ],\n755\t        \"note\": \"1000 bootstrap resamples (item × condition). CI width driven by 4-model limitation.\"\n756\t      },\n757\t      {\n758\t        \"name\": \"Table: IRT vs G-Theory Item Requirements\",\n759\t        \"columns\": [\n760\t          \"Benchmark\",\n761\t          \"IRT items\",\n762\t          \"G-theory items (G≥0.80)\",\n763\t          \"Ratio\",\n764\t          \"G at IRT count\"\n765\t        ],\n766\t        \"rows\": [\n767\t          [\n768\t            \"MMLU\",\n769\t            \"116\",\n770\t            \"414\",\n771\t            \"3.57×\",\n772\t            \"0.529\"\n773\t          ],\n774\t          [\n775\t            \"ARC\",\n776\t            \"105\",\n777\t            \"452\",\n778\t            \"4.30×\",\n779\t            \"0.498\"\n780\t          ],\n781\t          [\n782\t            \"HellaSwag\",\n783\t            \"98\",\n784\t            \"535\",\n785\t            \"5.46×\",\n786\t            \"0.412\"\n787\t          ],\n788\t          [\n789\t            \"GSM8K\",\n790\t            \"120\",\n791\t            \"488\",\n792\t            \"4.07×\",\n793\t            \"0.485\"\n794\t          ]\n795\t        ],\n796\t        \"note\": \"G-theory at IRT's recommended item count yields G=0.41-0.53 — far below 0.80 threshold\"\n797\t      },\n798\t      {\n799\t        \"name\": \"Table: D-Study Benchmark-Specific Budgets (Practical: T fixed)\",\n800\t        \"columns\": [\n801\t          \"Benchmark\",\n802\t          \"G≥0.80\",\n803\t          \"G≥0.80 CI\",\n804\t          \"G≥0.90\",\n805\t          \"G≥0.90 CI\",\n806\t          \"G≥0.95\",\n807\t          \"Prompts\",\n808\t          \"Seeds\"\n809\t        ],\n810\t        \"rows\": [\n811\t          [\n812\t            \"MMLU\",\n813\t            \"414\",\n814\t            \"[350, 490]\",\n815\t            \"510\",\n816\t            \"[430, 610]\",\n817\t            \"720\",\n818\t            \"3\",\n819\t            \"3\"\n820\t          ],\n821\t          [\n822\t            \"ARC\",\n823\t            \"452\",\n824\t            \"[375, 540]\",\n825\t            \"555\",\n826\t            \"[465, 665]\",\n827\t            \"780\",\n828\t            \"3\",\n829\t            \"3\"\n830\t          ],\n831\t          [\n832\t            \"HellaSwag\",\n833\t            \"535\",\n834\t            \"[440, 645]\",\n835\t            \"660\",\n836\t            \"[545, 795]\",\n837\t            \"930\",\n838\t            \"4\",\n839\t            \"4\"\n840\t          ],\n841\t          [\n842\t            \"GSM8K\",\n843\t            \"488\",\n844\t            \"[400, 590]\",\n845\t            \"600\",\n846\t            \"[495, 720]\",\n847\t            \"845\",\n848\t            \"4\",\n849\t            \"4\"\n850\t          ],\n851\t          [\n852\t            \"MATH\",\n853\t            \"582\",\n854\t            \"[470, 710]\",\n855\t            \"720\",\n856\t            \"[585, 875]\",\n857\t            \"1015\",\n858\t            \"4\",\n859\t            \"4\"\n860\t          ]\n861\t        ]\n862\t      },\n863\t      {\n864\t        \"name\": \"Table: Scoring Metric Comparison (MMLU, 4-Model)\",\n865\t        \"columns\": [\n866\t          \"Source\",\n867\t          \"Binary\",\n868\t          \"Logprob\",\n869\t          \"Text-exact\"\n870\t        ],\n871\t        \"rows\": [\n872\t          [\n873\t            \"item_id\",\n874\t            \"42.1%\",\n875\t            \"55.2%\",\n876\t            \"3.1%\"\n877\t          ],\n878\t          [\n879\t            \"model×item\",\n880\t            \"33.6%\",\n881\t            \"26.8%\",\n882\t            \"1.5%\"\n883\t          ],\n884\t          [\n885\t            \"prompt×item\",\n886\t            \"3.2%\",\n887\t            \"2.5%\",\n888\t            \"34.5%\"\n889\t          ],\n890\t          [\n891\t            \"residual\",\n892\t            \"12.3%\",\n893\t            \"5.8%\",\n894\t            \"38.2%\"\n895\t          ],\n896\t          [\n897\t            \"G_item\",\n898\t            \"0.820\",\n899\t            \"0.875\",\n900\t            \"0.006\"\n901\t          ]\n902\t        ]\n903\t      },\n904\t      {\n905\t        \"name\": \"Table: Methodological Robustness Summary\",\n906\t        \"columns\": [\n907\t          \"Analysis\",\n908\t          \"Result\",\n909\t          \"Conclusion\"\n910\t        ],\n911\t        \"rows\": [\n912\t          [\n913\t            \"REML vs Henderson I\",\n914\t            \"Max diff 0.45pp, all rankings preserved\",\n915\t            \"Henderson I adequate for balanced design\"\n916\t          ],\n917\t          [\n918\t            \"Fixed vs random (temp/ordering)\",\n919\t            \"Max change 1.8pp\",\n920\t            \"Conclusions robust to facet classification\"\n921\t          ],\n922\t          [\n923\t            \"Bootstrap vs jackknife CIs\",\n924\t            \"Width ratio 0.94–1.06\",\n925\t            \"Independence violation negligible\"\n926\t          ],\n927\t          [\n928\t            \"Design asymmetry (3×3 vs 2×2)\",\n929\t            \"Δ = 0.7pp on MMLU\",\n930\t            \"Reduced design adequate\"\n931\t          ],\n932\t          [\n933\t            \"Null simulation (binary)\",\n934\t            \"Obs/null ratio = 526×\",\n935\t            \"Binary G-theory findings are not artifact\"\n936\t          ],\n937\t          [\n938\t            \"Full-benchmark G projection\",\n939\t            \"G = 0.94–0.99 at full size\",\n940\t            \"Subsampling is the reliability bottleneck\"\n941\t          ]\n942\t        ]\n943\t      }\n944\t    ],\n945\t    \"figures\": [],\n946\t    \"analysis\": \"exp-004 is the analytical backbone of the paper. Five findings for AAAI framing: (1) IRT vs G-theory ratio of 3.6-5.5× across all benchmarks — this is the \\\"cost of multi-facet reliability\\\" contribution, now confirmed cross-benchmark. (2) Bootstrap CIs show model×item uncertainty is the limiting factor; the paper must honestly report that 4 models provides only rough magnitude estimates (±5pp). (3) D-study budgets are benchmark-conditional with CIs that overlap substantially (MMLU [350,490] vs GSM8K [400,590]) — the practical message is \\\"400-600 items for any benchmark\\\" rather than sharply differentiated budgets. (4) Logprob scoring strengthens the metric-conditional narrative: item_id rises from 42% to 55% under continuous scoring, confirming that binary 0/1 compresses item-level information. (5) All methodological robustness checks pass: REML, fixed-vs-random, bootstrap-vs-jackknife, design asymmetry, null simulation. The paper's Methodological Defense package is complete.\\n\\n\\nBootstrap CIs reveal that model×item is the most uncertain component (±5pp) because 4 model levels yield only 3 df for variance estimation — this is the fundamental statistical limitation of the current design. Gradient endpoints overlap: MMLU lower CI (36.0%) meets GSM8K upper CI (37.8%), making the gradient directionally robust (p=0.003) but imprecise in magnitude — the paper must say \\\"10-20pp spread\\\" not \\\"16.3pp.\\\" D-study CIs are correspondingly wide: MMLU G≥0.80 requires 350-490 items depending on bootstrap sample. IRT comparison is one of the strongest findings: the 3.6-5.5× item ratio is consistent across all benchmarks and has a clean causal explanation (prompt×item + seed×item + residual dimensions that IRT ignores). HellaSwag has the worst ratio (5.46×) because its high prompt×item and seed×item inflate the G-theory budget disproportionately. REML confirms Henderson I within 0.45pp across all benchmarks — methodological choice is not a concern. Logprob scoring increases item_id to 52-55% because the continuous signal captures fine-grained difficulty (items at 0.55 vs 0.65 logprob difficulty are distinguishable, unlike binary 1/1). Fixed vs random sensitivity shows <2pp change, validating the mixed-model approach. Design asymmetry check (MMLU 3×3 vs 2×2 matched) shows only 0.7pp difference, confirming exp-002's reduced design is adequate.\\n\"\n947\t  },\n948\t  {\n949\t    \"name\": \"14B Model Scale Extension\",\n950\t    \"description\": \"P1 priority. Blocked on exp-003 (descoped) — dependency can be removed if run independently at BF16 only. Qwen3-14B + DeepSeek-R1-Distill-14B on MMLU and GSM8K with reduced design: BF16 × 2 temps × 4 prompts × 4 seeds × 2 orderings × 200 items.\\n\",\n951\t    \"results\": {\n952\t      \"status\": \"planned — not started, blocked on hardware availability\",\n953\t      \"qwen3_14b_mmlu_accuracy\": 0.752,\n954\t      \"deepseek_r1_14b_mmlu_accuracy\": 0.735,\n955\t      \"qwen3_14b_gsm8k_accuracy\": 0.845,\n956\t      \"deepseek_r1_14b_gsm8k_accuracy\": 0.812,\n957\t      \"mmlu_item_id_14b_2model\": 38.5,\n958\t      \"mmlu_model_x_item_14b\": 28.2,\n959\t      \"gsm8k_item_id_14b_2model\": 28.5,\n960\t      \"gsm8k_model_x_item_14b\": 35.8,\n961\t      \"variance_hierarchy_preserved\": true,\n962\t      \"item_id_8b_vs_14b_diff_pp\": -3.5,\n963\t      \"deepseek_r1_temp_sensitivity_elevated\": true,\n964\t      \"deepseek_r1_temp_x_item_gsm8k\": 8.5\n965\t    },\n966\t    \"tables\": [\n967\t      {\n968\t        \"name\": \"Table: 8B vs 14B Variance Structure (MMLU, BF16)\",\n969\t        \"columns\": [\n970\t          \"Source\",\n971\t          \"8B (4 models)\",\n972\t          \"14B (2 models)\",\n973\t          \"Δ\"\n974\t        ],\n975\t        \"rows\": [\n976\t          [\n977\t            \"item_id\",\n978\t            \"42.1%\",\n979\t            \"38.5%\",\n980\t            \"-3.6pp\"\n981\t          ],\n982\t          [\n983\t            \"model×item\",\n984\t            \"33.6%\",\n985\t            \"28.2%\",\n986\t            \"-5.4pp\"\n987\t          ],\n988\t          [\n989\t            \"residual\",\n990\t            \"12.3%\",\n991\t            \"18.5%\",\n992\t            \"+6.2pp\"\n993\t          ]\n994\t        ],\n995\t        \"note\": \"14B model×item appears lower than 8B but is confounded by N=2 models (high residual absorbs signal)\"\n996\t      }\n997\t    ],\n998\t    \"figures\": [],\n999\t    \"analysis\": \"Useful for Discussion if compute permits, but not essential for AAAI submission. The key finding (item_id stable, hierarchy preserved) is expected from measurement theory — contribution is confirming the expectation empirically. Low priority given timeline pressure.\\n\\n\\n14B models would show ~3.5pp lower item_id than 8B because higher capacity reduces floor effects — items impossible for 8B become solvable at 14B, compressing between-item variance. model×item rises because dense (Qwen3-14B) vs reasoning-distilled (DeepSeek-R1-Distill-14B) architectures create larger model-specific item profiles: DeepSeek excels on multi-step reasoning items (distilled from R1's chain-of-thought traces), Qwen excels on factual knowledge. DeepSeek shows elevated temperature×item on GSM8K (~8.5%) because reasoning- distilled models produce branching chain-of-thought that is more sampling- sensitive. Only 2 models limits statistical power — model×item estimates would have very wide CIs. Position as Discussion-section scale validation, not a primary finding. The practical implication: variance hierarchy is stable at 7-14B, suggesting much larger models (70B+) would be needed to alter the structure.\\n\"\n1000\t  },\n1001\t  {\n1002\t    \"name\": \"Fine-Tuning G-Study (RoBERTa)\",\n1003\t    \"description\": \"P1 priority, independent of exp-003. RoBERTa-large on SST-2/MNLI/RTE/COPA. 6 seeds × 3 LRs × 4 data shuffles × 3 GPUs × 2 precisions = 432 runs/task × 4 tasks = 1,728 fine-tuning runs. Validates whether variance hierarchy differs between inference and fine-tuning.\\n\",\n1004\t    \"results\": {\n1005\t      \"status\": \"planned — not started (200 GPU hours, P1)\",\n1006\t      \"total_fine_tuning_runs\": 1728,\n1007\t      \"variance_decomposition_summary\": {\n1008\t        \"SST2\": {\n1009\t          \"dominant\": \"learning_rate (32%)\",\n1010\t          \"second\": \"seed (24%)\",\n1011\t          \"third\": \"data_shuffle (13%)\",\n1012\t          \"seed_x_lr\": \"11%\",\n1013\t          \"gpu\": \"0.3%\",\n1014\t          \"precision\": \"0.8%\",\n1015\t          \"residual\": \"18.9%\"\n1016\t        },\n1017\t        \"MNLI\": {\n1018\t          \"dominant\": \"learning_rate (28%)\",\n1019\t          \"second\": \"seed (22%)\",\n1020\t          \"third\": \"data_shuffle (16%)\",\n1021\t          \"seed_x_lr\": \"12%\",\n1022\t          \"gpu\": \"0.4%\",\n1023\t          \"precision\": \"0.9%\",\n1024\t          \"residual\": \"20.7%\"\n1025\t        },\n1026\t        \"RTE\": {\n1027\t          \"dominant\": \"data_shuffle (26%)\",\n1028\t          \"second\": \"learning_rate (20%)\",\n1029\t          \"third\": \"seed×lr (15%)\",\n1030\t          \"seed\": \"14%\",\n1031\t          \"gpu\": \"0.5%\",\n1032\t          \"precision\": \"1.0%\",\n1033\t          \"residual\": \"23.5%\"\n1034\t        },\n1035\t        \"COPA\": {\n1036\t          \"dominant\": \"data_shuffle (30%)\",\n1037\t          \"second\": \"seed (20%)\",\n1038\t          \"third\": \"learning_rate (16%)\",\n1039\t          \"seed_x_lr\": \"12%\",\n1040\t          \"gpu\": \"0.4%\",\n1041\t          \"precision\": \"1.2%\",\n1042\t          \"residual\": \"20.4%\"\n1043\t        }\n1044\t      },\n1045\t      \"hierarchy_differs_from_inference\": true,\n1046\t      \"infrastructure_negligible_both_modes\": true,\n1047\t      \"rte_bimodal_seed_lr\": true,\n1048\t      \"rte_bimodal_gap_pp\": 4.2\n1049\t    },\n1050\t    \"tables\": [\n1051\t      {\n1052\t        \"name\": \"Table: Inference vs Fine-Tuning Variance Hierarchy\",\n1053\t        \"columns\": [\n1054\t          \"Rank\",\n1055\t          \"Inference (MMLU)\",\n1056\t          \"FT-Large (SST-2)\",\n1057\t          \"FT-Small (RTE)\"\n1058\t        ],\n1059\t        \"rows\": [\n1060\t          [\n1061\t            \"#1\",\n1062\t            \"item_id (42%)\",\n1063\t            \"learning_rate (32%)\",\n1064\t            \"data_shuffle (26%)\"\n1065\t          ],\n1066\t          [\n1067\t            \"#2\",\n1068\t            \"model×item (34%)\",\n1069\t            \"seed (24%)\",\n1070\t            \"learning_rate (20%)\"\n1071\t          ],\n1072\t          [\n1073\t            \"#3\",\n1074\t            \"residual (12%)\",\n1075\t            \"residual (19%)\",\n1076\t            \"seed×lr (15%)\"\n1077\t          ],\n1078\t          [\n1079\t            \"Infra total\",\n1080\t            \"precision <0.5%\",\n1081\t            \"gpu+prec 1.1%\",\n1082\t            \"gpu+prec 1.5%\"\n1083\t          ]\n1084\t        ]\n1085\t      }\n1086\t    ],\n1087\t    \"figures\": [],\n1088\t    \"analysis\": \"Downgraded per Dream #3 directive to Discussion-section preliminary observation. The finding that infrastructure is negligible in BOTH inference and fine-tuning strengthens Claim 2, but this is encoder-only and cannot support broad claims. If AAAI timeline is tight, this experiment is the first to cut. Worth doing for ACL ARR October if time permits.\\n\\n\\nFine-tuning variance is qualitatively different from inference: hyperparameters (LR, seed, data shuffle) dominate instead of items. On large datasets (SST-2, MNLI), learning rate dominates (28-32%) because the optimization landscape is well-defined and LR determines convergence basin. On small datasets (RTE 277 examples, COPA 400 examples), data shuffle dominates (26-30%) because mini-batch composition has outsized influence with fewer training examples — a single hard example in early batches steers the model into a different loss basin. seed×LR interaction (11-15%) creates bimodal accuracy on RTE: two loss basins separated by ~4pp, consistent with Dodge et al. (2020) and Bui et al. (2025). GPU and precision effects remain negligible (<1.2%) — the infrastructure-is-negligible finding generalizes from inference to fine-tuning. Frame as Discussion-section preliminary finding showing G-theory generality. Explicit caveat: encoder-only fine-tuning (RoBERTa) may not generalize to decoder fine-tuning.\\n\"\n1089\t  },\n1090\t  {\n1091\t    \"name\": \"LayerCast Precision Mitigation\",\n1092\t    \"description\": \"P2 priority. LayerCast (FP16 storage + FP32 compute) as additional precision condition on MMLU with 4 models.\\n\",\n1093\t    \"results\": {\n1094\t      \"status\": \"planned — not started (30 GPU hours, P2)\",\n1095\t      \"layercast_accuracy\": 0.713,\n1096\t      \"layercast_vs_bf16_gap_pp\": 0.2,\n1097\t      \"precision_x_item_layercast_pct\": 0.02,\n1098\t      \"inference_overhead_pct\": 18,\n1099\t      \"g_coefficient_unchanged\": true\n1100\t    },\n1101\t    \"tables\": [],\n1102\t    \"figures\": [],\n1103\t    \"analysis\": \"Lowest priority. Skip for AAAI unless reviewer explicitly asks about precision mitigation strategies. The BF16-vs-FP16 sensitivity analysis from exp-001 already shows precision is a non-issue for practical evaluation (0.0006% variance after excluding FP32).\\n\\n\\nLayerCast reduces precision×item from BF16's already-negligible 0.04% (post BF16-vs-FP16 sensitivity analysis) to ~0.02% — the improvement is unmeasurable in practice. With BF16≈FP16 (Δ=0.23pp from exp-001) and precision contributing <0.1% of variance, any mitigation strategy provides diminishing returns. The 18% inference overhead makes LayerCast cost-ineffective. Position as 1-paragraph appendix material if run; otherwise not worth the GPU hours given AAAI timeline.\\n\"\n1104\t  },\n1105\t  {\n1106\t    \"name\": \"MATH Benchmark\",\n1107\t    \"description\": \"Merged into exp-002 Phase 2. All results included in exp-002 predictions above.\",\n1108\t    \"results\": {\n1109\t      \"status\": \"merged_into_exp002\",\n1110\t      \"see\": \"exp-002 MATH results (3-model preliminary)\"\n1111\t    },\n1112\t    \"tables\": [],\n1113\t    \"figures\": [],\n1114\t    \"analysis\": \"See exp-002.\\n\\nNo standalone experiment — MATH data collected as part of exp-002 Phase 2.\"\n1115\t  }\n1116\t]"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"20f76664-8d08-43f7-a19b-5ac1c53e3195","uuid":"56e423e1-ab8b-4ae2-bf51-a14495a3c446","timestamp":"2026-05-21T13:17:53.768Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0519/projects/nlp_variance_gtheory/artifacts/dream_reports/dream_20260521T122449/median/experiment_data.json","content":"[\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Multi-Benchmark G-Study (Phase 1-2 + Phase 3 partial)\",\n    \"description\": \"Phase 1 DONE: 4 original models × 4 benchmarks (MMLU/ARC-C/HellaSwag/GSM8K), BF16 × 2 temps (0.0, 0.7) × 6 prompts × 6 seeds × 4 orderings × 200 items. Phase 2 DONE: 4 models × MATH (5th benchmark), same reduced design. Phase 3 partial: Yi-1.5-9B completed on MMLU+ARC; OLMo-2-7B completed on MMLU. MMLU data reused from exp-001 BF16 subset (no new collection needed). Total new data: ~1.10M records (Phase 1-2) + ~173K (Phase 3 partial) = ~1.27M.\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"completion_status\": \"Phase 1-2 done, Phase 3 ~20%\",\n      \"total_records_new\": 1267200,\n      \"total_records_with_exp001_mmlu_reuse\": 1324800,\n      \"n_models_primary\": 4,\n      \"n_models_total\": 6,\n      \"n_benchmarks\": 5,\n      \"gpu_hours_used\": 258,\n      \"per_benchmark_accuracy_bf16_mean\": {\n        \"MMLU\": {\n          \"overall\": 0.711,\n          \"Llama\": 0.711,\n          \"Gemma\": 0.76,\n          \"Qwen\": 0.726,\n          \"Mistral\": 0.67,\n          \"spread_pp\": 9.0\n        },\n        \"ARC\": {\n          \"overall\": 0.785,\n          \"Llama\": 0.79,\n          \"Gemma\": 0.848,\n          \"Qwen\": 0.818,\n          \"Mistral\": 0.682,\n          \"spread_pp\": 16.6\n        },\n        \"HellaSwag\": {\n          \"overall\": 0.815,\n          \"Llama\": 0.812,\n          \"Gemma\": 0.852,\n          \"Qwen\": 0.838,\n          \"Mistral\": 0.758,\n          \"spread_pp\": 9.4\n        },\n        \"GSM8K\": {\n          \"overall\": 0.645,\n          \"Llama\": 0.615,\n          \"Gemma\": 0.68,\n          \"Qwen\": 0.78,\n          \"Mistral\": 0.485,\n          \"spread_pp\": 29.5\n        },\n        \"MATH\": {\n          \"overall\": 0.283,\n          \"Llama\": 0.218,\n          \"Gemma\": 0.278,\n          \"Qwen\": 0.352,\n          \"Mistral\": \"pending_phase2_tail\",\n          \"spread_pp_3model\": 13.4\n        }\n      },\n      \"cross_model_variance_decomposition\": {\n        \"MMLU\": {\n          \"item_id\": 42.1,\n          \"model_x_item\": 33.6,\n          \"model\": 3.8,\n          \"prompt_x_item\": 3.2,\n          \"seed_x_item\": 2.6,\n          \"temperature_x_item\": 1.2,\n          \"prompt\": 0.5,\n          \"temperature\": 0.2,\n          \"seed\": 0.1,\n          \"model_x_prompt\": 0.3,\n          \"model_x_temperature\": 0.1,\n          \"ordering\": 0.05,\n          \"residual\": 12.25\n        },\n        \"ARC\": {\n          \"item_id\": 37.8,\n          \"model_x_item\": 34.5,\n          \"model\": 5.5,\n          \"prompt_x_item\": 3.8,\n          \"seed_x_item\": 2.3,\n          \"temperature_x_item\": 1.6,\n          \"prompt\": 0.9,\n          \"temperature\": 0.3,\n          \"seed\": 0.1,\n          \"model_x_prompt\": 0.5,\n          \"model_x_temperature\": 0.2,\n          \"ordering\": 0.1,\n          \"residual\": 12.4\n        },\n        \"HellaSwag\": {\n          \"item_id\": 29.5,\n          \"model_x_item\": 32.8,\n          \"model\": 3.2,\n          \"prompt_x_item\": 6.2,\n          \"seed_x_item\": 4.5,\n          \"temperature_x_item\": 2.5,\n          \"prompt\": 1.8,\n          \"temperature\": 0.5,\n          \"seed\": 0.2,\n          \"model_x_prompt\": 0.8,\n          \"model_x_temperature\": 0.1,\n          \"ordering\": 0.1,\n          \"residual\": 17.8\n        },\n        \"GSM8K\": {\n          \"item_id\": 31.2,\n          \"model_x_item\": 36.2,\n          \"model\": 10.5,\n          \"prompt_x_item\": 4.5,\n          \"seed_x_item\": 2.8,\n          \"temperature_x_item\": 1.8,\n          \"prompt\": 1.2,\n          \"temperature\": 0.4,\n          \"seed\": 0.2,\n          \"model_x_prompt\": 0.5,\n          \"model_x_temperature\": 0.3,\n          \"ordering\": 0.1,\n          \"residual\": 10.3\n        },\n        \"MATH_3model\": {\n          \"item_id\": 25.8,\n          \"model_x_item\": 38.5,\n          \"model\": 6.5,\n          \"prompt_x_item\": 5.8,\n          \"seed_x_item\": 4.2,\n          \"temperature_x_item\": 2.8,\n          \"prompt\": 2.0,\n          \"temperature\": 0.8,\n          \"seed\": 0.3,\n          \"model_x_prompt\": 0.6,\n          \"model_x_temperature\": 0.2,\n          \"ordering\": 0.1,\n          \"residual\": 12.4\n        }\n      },\n      \"single_model_item_id_Llama\": {\n        \"MMLU\": 65.2,\n        \"ARC\": 58.0,\n        \"HellaSwag\": 50.2,\n        \"GSM8K\": 56.5,\n        \"MATH\": 48.0\n      },\n      \"single_to_cross_item_id_drop_pp\": {\n        \"MMLU\": -23.1,\n        \"ARC\": -20.2,\n        \"HellaSwag\": -20.7,\n        \"GSM8K\": -25.3,\n        \"MATH\": -22.2\n      },\n      \"item_id_by_hypothesized_complexity_order\": \"MMLU(42.1) > ARC(37.8) > HellaSwag(29.5) < GSM8K(31.2) > MATH(25.8)\",\n      \"gradient_break\": \"HellaSwag(29.5) < GSM8K(31.2) — HellaSwag drops below GSM8K despite lower task complexity\",\n      \"gradient_spread_pp\": 16.3,\n      \"gradient_monotonicity_permutation_p\": 0.12,\n      \"gradient_monotonicity_interpretation\": \"Directional trend exists but not statistically monotonic at α=0.05\",\n      \"format_confound\": {\n        \"MC_mean_item_id\": 40.0,\n        \"completion_item_id\": 29.5,\n        \"free_form_mean_item_id\": 28.5,\n        \"MC_vs_nonMC_gap_pp\": 11.0,\n        \"within_MC_gradient_pp\": 4.3,\n        \"within_free_form_gradient_pp\": 5.4,\n        \"within_format_conclusion\": \"weak_or_inconclusive — direction consistent but N=2 per format, insufficient for statistical test\"\n      },\n      \"G_item_cross_model\": {\n        \"MMLU\": 0.82,\n        \"ARC\": 0.783,\n        \"HellaSwag\": 0.723,\n        \"GSM8K\": 0.736,\n        \"MATH_3model\": 0.698\n      },\n      \"D_study_items_G80\": {\n        \"MMLU\": 414,\n        \"ARC\": 452,\n        \"HellaSwag\": 535,\n        \"GSM8K\": 488,\n        \"MATH\": 582\n      },\n      \"D_study_range\": \"414–582 items\",\n      \"per_model_interaction_pct\": {\n        \"MMLU\": {\n          \"Mistral\": 29.25,\n          \"Qwen\": 27.11,\n          \"Gemma\": 23.95,\n          \"Llama\": 19.69\n        },\n        \"ARC\": {\n          \"Mistral\": 32.8,\n          \"Gemma\": 25.5,\n          \"Qwen\": 23.2,\n          \"Llama\": 18.5\n        },\n        \"HellaSwag\": {\n          \"Mistral\": 30.5,\n          \"Llama\": 26.2,\n          \"Qwen\": 24.8,\n          \"Gemma\": 18.5\n        },\n        \"GSM8K\": {\n          \"Mistral\": 35.2,\n          \"Llama\": 30.5,\n          \"Gemma\": 22.8,\n          \"Qwen\": 11.5\n        }\n      },\n      \"phase3_5model_mmlu\": {\n        \"Yi_accuracy_bf16\": 0.652,\n        \"item_id_5model\": 41.2,\n        \"model_x_item_5model\": 35.0,\n        \"G_item_5model\": 0.842,\n        \"D_study_predicted_5model\": 0.848,\n        \"D_study_delta\": 0.006,\n        \"D_study_validation\": \"Second out-of-sample validation: 4-model D-study predicted G=0.848 for 5 models, observed 0.842, Δ=0.006\"\n      }\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table: Cross-Benchmark Variance Decomposition (4 Models, BF16, Binary)\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Source\",\n          \"MMLU\",\n          \"ARC\",\n          \"HellaSwag\",\n          \"GSM8K\",\n          \"MATH†\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"item_id\",\n            \"42.1%\",\n            \"37.8%\",\n            \"29.5%\",\n            \"31.2%\",\n            \"25.8%\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"model×item\",\n            \"33.6%\",\n            \"34.5%\",\n            \"32.8%\",\n            \"36.2%\",\n            \"38.5%\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"model\",\n            \"3.8%\",\n            \"5.5%\",\n            \"3.2%\",\n            \"10.5%\",\n            \"6.5%\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"prompt×item\",\n            \"3.2%\",\n            \"3.8%\",\n            \"6.2%\",\n            \"4.5%\",\n            \"5.8%\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"seed×item\",\n            \"2.6%\",\n            \"2.3%\",\n            \"4.5%\",\n            \"2.8%\",\n            \"4.2%\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"temp×item\",\n            \"1.2%\",\n            \"1.6%\",\n            \"2.5%\",\n            \"1.8%\",\n            \"2.8%\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"residual\",\n            \"12.3%\",\n            \"12.4%\",\n            \"17.8%\",\n            \"10.3%\",\n            \"12.4%\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"other (main+2-way)\",\n            \"1.2%\",\n            \"2.1%\",\n            \"3.5%\",\n            \"2.7%\",\n            \"4.0%\"\n          ]\n        ],\n        \"note\": \"†MATH uses 3-model preliminary data (Mistral pending). MMLU from exp-001 BF16 subset.\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table: Gradient Summary and Format Confound\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Benchmark\",\n          \"Format\",\n          \"item_id%\",\n          \"model×item%\",\n          \"G_item\",\n          \"D-study G≥0.80\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"MMLU\",\n            \"4-choice MC\",\n            \"42.1%\",\n            \"33.6%\",\n            \"0.820\",\n            \"414 items\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"ARC-C\",\n            \"4-choice MC\",\n            \"37.8%\",\n            \"34.5%\",\n            \"0.783\",\n            \"452 items\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"GSM8K\",\n            \"Free-form\",\n            \"31.2%\",\n            \"36.2%\",\n            \"0.736\",\n            \"488 items\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"HellaSwag\",\n            \"4-choice completion\",\n            \"29.5%\",\n            \"32.8%\",\n            \"0.723\",\n            \"535 items\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"MATH†\",\n            \"Free-form\",\n            \"25.8%\",\n            \"38.5%\",\n            \"0.698\",\n            \"582 items\"\n          ]\n        ],\n        \"note\": \"Permutation test for monotonic decrease along hypothesized complexity ordering: p=0.12\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table: Single-Model → Cross-Model item_id Drop\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Benchmark\",\n          \"Single (Llama)\",\n          \"Cross (4-model)\",\n          \"Δ (pp)\",\n          \"model×item absorbed\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"MMLU\",\n            \"65.2%\",\n            \"42.1%\",\n            \"-23.1\",\n            \"33.6%\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"ARC\",\n            \"58.0%\",\n            \"37.8%\",\n            \"-20.2\",\n            \"34.5%\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"HellaSwag\",\n            \"50.2%\",\n            \"29.5%\",\n            \"-20.7\",\n            \"32.8%\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"GSM8K\",\n            \"56.5%\",\n            \"31.2%\",\n            \"-25.3\",\n            \"36.2%\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"MATH\",\n            \"48.0%\",\n            \"25.8%\",\n            \"-22.2\",\n            \"38.5%\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table: Per-Model Accuracy by Benchmark (BF16, T=0.0)\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Model\",\n          \"MMLU\",\n          \"ARC\",\n          \"HellaSwag\",\n          \"GSM8K\",\n          \"MATH\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"Llama-3.1-8B\",\n            \"0.711\",\n            \"0.790\",\n            \"0.812\",\n            \"0.615\",\n            \"0.218\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Gemma-2-9B\",\n            \"0.760\",\n            \"0.848\",\n            \"0.852\",\n            \"0.680\",\n            \"0.278\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Qwen3-8B\",\n            \"0.726\",\n            \"0.818\",\n            \"0.838\",\n            \"0.780\",\n            \"0.352\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Mistral-7B\",\n            \"0.670\",\n            \"0.682\",\n            \"0.758\",\n            \"0.485\",\n            \"—\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Yi-1.5-9B*\",\n            \"0.652\",\n            \"0.735\",\n            \"—\",\n            \"—\",\n            \"—\"\n          ]\n        ],\n        \"note\": \"*Phase 3 partial. OLMo-2-7B completed MMLU only (0.618).\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"The gradient is the paper's primary novel finding but requires careful framing in median tier. The 16.3pp spread (MMLU 42.1% → MATH 25.8%) is real but the non-monotonicity at HellaSwag→GSM8K (p=0.12) means the paper cannot claim a 'systematic monotonic gradient.' Instead: 'benchmark-conditional variance structure with task-type as a partial predictor, confounded with evaluation format.' The MC/non-MC clustering (11pp gap) is the more defensible finding: evaluation format partially determines variance structure independent of task content. Within-format gradient is too weak to draw conclusions (4.3pp within MC, 5.4pp within free-form, N=2 each). model×item as the second-largest source is confirmed across ALL 5 benchmarks (32.8-38.5%), strengthening the exp-001 MMLU finding. D-study validation replicates with Yi (Δ=0.006). Precision separability cannot be tested cross-benchmark (exp-002 is BF16-only) — this limits Claim 2 to MMLU evidence from exp-001. MATH 3-model data is preliminary; Mistral completion would likely push MATH model×item above 40% given Mistral's expected ~12% accuracy. For AAAI: the gradient+format confound story is publishable with softened claims, but the HellaSwag anomaly will draw reviewer scrutiny — prepare Discussion paragraph explaining completion format's effect on variance structure.\\n\\n\\nGradient exists but is noisy because HellaSwag (completion format, 29.5%) drops below GSM8K (free-form math, 31.2%) in item_id%. The hypothesized knowledge→reasoning gradient predicts HellaSwag should be intermediate between ARC and GSM8K, but HellaSwag's completion format drives its item_id lower than expected: the 4-choice completion paradigm introduces more model-specific pattern-matching variance (prompt×item 6.2%, seed×item 4.5%) than MC or free-form formats, compressing the item_id share. GSM8K retains relatively high item_id (31.2%) because math items have very clear universal difficulty structure — trivial arithmetic vs impossible multi-step problems — creating a floor of item-driven variance that persists even cross-model. The format confound is partial: MC benchmarks (MMLU 40.0%, ARC 37.8%) cluster 11pp above non-MC (29.0% mean), but within-format gradients are only 4-5pp with N=2 per format, insufficient to disentangle format from task-type. model×item ranges from 32.8% (HellaSwag) to 38.5% (MATH 3-model), increasing on reasoning benchmarks but not consistently — HellaSwag's model×item (32.8%) is slightly below MMLU's (33.6%), breaking the monotonic increase pattern. GSM8K's model main effect (10.5%) is 2.8× MMLU's (3.8%), driven by Mistral's dramatically lower math performance (48.5% vs 78.0% for Qwen) — this large model spread inflates the model component and correspondingly depresses residual (10.3% vs 12.3% on MMLU). MATH (3-model preliminary) shows the lowest item_id (25.8%) and highest model×item (38.5%), consistent with the gradient direction but the 3-model estimate has wider CI than 4-model benchmarks. The D-study validation replicates: 4-model D-study predicted G=0.848 for 5 models on MMLU, observed 0.842 with Yi added (Δ=0.006), consistent with the exp-001 out-of-sample Δ=0.004. D-study budgets vary from 414 (MMLU) to 582 (MATH) items for G≥0.80, but this variation is partially confounded with benchmark design properties (item difficulty distribution, accuracy floor effects) rather than purely task-type. HellaSwag's high budget (535) despite moderate item_id is driven by its large prompt×item (6.2%) and seed×item (4.5%) which inflate the error term in the G-coefficient denominator.\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Multi-Hardware G-Study\",\n    \"description\": \"DESCOPED — hardware TBD. Predictions below are conditional on obtaining a second GPU type (e.g., A100-80GB or H100). Design: 4 models × 2 GPU types × 2 precisions (BF16, FP16) × 6 prompts × 6 seeds × 3 temperatures × 4 orderings × 200 MMLU items.\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"status\": \"descoped — no second GPU type available\",\n      \"total_records_if_run\": 1152000,\n      \"hardware_main_binary_pct\": 0.3,\n      \"hardware_x_precision_binary_pct\": 0.8,\n      \"hardware_x_item_binary_pct\": 1.5,\n      \"total_hardware_related_binary_pct\": 3.2,\n      \"cross_gpu_gap_bf16_mean_pp\": 0.12,\n      \"cross_gpu_gap_fp16_mean_pp\": 0.65,\n      \"model_ranking_preserved\": true,\n      \"item_id_with_hardware_binary_pct\": 41.0\n    },\n    \"tables\": [],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Descoped. Paper must explicitly scope Claim 2: \\\"numerical precision separability on a single GPU architecture (RTX PRO 6000).\\\" Hardware crossing is natural future work. The BF16≈FP16 finding from exp-001 (Δ=0.23pp) provides indirect evidence that hardware effects would be negligible for BF16, since BF16's 8-bit exponent provides hardware-independent dynamic range.\\n\\n\\nHardware effects would be small (total ~3.2% binary) because both GPU types implement identical IEEE 754 operations; differences arise from CUDA kernel scheduling nondeterminism and memory subsystem timing. FP16 would show 5× larger hardware sensitivity than BF16 (0.65pp vs 0.12pp cross-GPU gap) because FP16's narrower dynamic range makes accumulation order hardware-dependent. This would strengthen Claim 2 by extending \\\"precision separability\\\" to \\\"hardware separability\\\" — but the experiment is descoped because infrastructure claim was already narrowed to precision per D003/D007. Without this experiment, Claim 2 remains scoped to \\\"precision on single GPU architecture.\\\"\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Comprehensive Combined Analysis\",\n    \"description\": \"Pure analysis (no GPU). Depends on exp-001 (DONE) + exp-002 (Phase 1-2 DONE). 17 sub-analyses covering bootstrap CIs, D-study projections, REML comparison, IRT vs G-theory, logprob scoring, fixed-vs-random sensitivity, binary data validation, power analysis, GPU cost, and practitioner toolkit.\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"model_as_facet_note\": \"Already incorporated in exp-002 cross-model decomposition\",\n      \"bootstrap_CIs_95pct\": {\n        \"MMLU\": {\n          \"item_id\": [\n            36.0,\n            48.8\n          ],\n          \"model_x_item\": [\n            28.4,\n            37.9\n          ],\n          \"model\": [\n            1.2,\n            7.5\n          ]\n        },\n        \"ARC\": {\n          \"item_id\": [\n            31.5,\n            44.2\n          ],\n          \"model_x_item\": [\n            29.0,\n            39.8\n          ],\n          \"model\": [\n            2.0,\n            10.2\n          ]\n        },\n        \"HellaSwag\": {\n          \"item_id\": [\n            23.8,\n            35.5\n          ],\n          \"model_x_item\": [\n            27.5,\n            38.2\n          ],\n          \"model\": [\n            0.8,\n            6.8\n          ]\n        },\n        \"GSM8K\": {\n          \"item_id\": [\n            25.0,\n            37.8\n          ],\n          \"model_x_item\": [\n            30.5,\n            41.8\n          ],\n          \"model\": [\n            5.2,\n            16.5\n          ]\n        },\n        \"MATH_3model\": {\n          \"item_id\": [\n            19.2,\n            33.0\n          ],\n          \"model_x_item\": [\n            31.5,\n            45.2\n          ],\n          \"model\": [\n            2.5,\n            11.5\n          ]\n        }\n      },\n      \"gradient_endpoint_CI_overlap\": \"MMLU lower bound (36.0) overlaps with GSM8K upper bound (37.8) — gradient direction is robust (p=0.003 permutation) but magnitude is imprecise\",\n      \"model_x_item_CI_width_note\": \"Wide CIs (±5pp) on model×item reflect only 4 models; 8+ models would halve CI width\",\n      \"D_study_items_with_CI\": {\n        \"MMLU\": {\n          \"G80\": 414,\n          \"G80_CI\": [\n            350,\n            490\n          ],\n          \"G90\": 510,\n          \"G90_CI\": [\n            430,\n            610\n          ],\n          \"G95\": 720\n        },\n        \"ARC\": {\n          \"G80\": 452,\n          \"G80_CI\": [\n            375,\n            540\n          ],\n          \"G90\": 555,\n          \"G90_CI\": [\n            465,\n            665\n          ],\n          \"G95\": 780\n        },\n        \"HellaSwag\": {\n          \"G80\": 535,\n          \"G80_CI\": [\n            440,\n            645\n          ],\n          \"G90\": 660,\n  